			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <br>Lol. The world and the word are funny. Grandparents had furniture that could be passed down for generations. We have furniture made out of glue and wood chips that melts if you move on a rainy day or breaks if it's good weather. It's too damn heavy to move as you age too. Almost like it's made to be replaced ASAP and put cash in an offshore tax haven. Progress.</p>",
