			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@tomw/113594046281250206",
			"author": {
				"name": "Tom Walker",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@tomw",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/338/280/995/838/214/original/fbcf1ae1c2f82118.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-12-04T10:19:50.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Even without the React/size thing, I frequently encounter people who simply will not use anything that was last updated 2018, because that means it's \"dead\". Only projects that are recently updated (even if it's updating the readme once a year) get used. I have no idea where this mindset comes from</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "113594091048439365",
			"parentId": "113594046375516467",
			"url": "https://tane.codes/@tanepiper/113594090252622422",
			"author": {
				"name": "Tane Piper ⁂",
				"url": "https://tane.codes/@tanepiper",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/293/774/936/514/785/original/c27131a82fd76715.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-12-04T10:31:01.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@tomw\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>tomw</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I do take a moment to check when I see this.  Also yes \"it hasn't been updated since 2018\" - but due to bad practices I have seen perfectly good dependencies light up the security board - one library shipped their entire Docker file with root setup and trivy did not like this.</p><p>FWIW I wrote a script that recursively cleans up node_modules - just deleting markdown files, configs and other stuff that should be in npm ignore cleans up 30-50mb of crap</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
